{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788220949,"nonce":"jJMFNHPX8j62avzw9USI1x14g6c=","message":"WORKER RESOLUTIONS — the three the shipped code already cites, plus the six\naudit fixes that follow from them. Written because the code says \"Resolved on\nthe issue\" and, until now, nothing on the issue resolved anything: this comment\nis what those citations point at.\n\n=====================================================================\nRESOLUTION 1 — BILL IDENTITY IS `uid`, AND `index` IS KEPT AS THE\nPOSITIONAL HANDLE IT ACTUALLY IS. BOTH ARE PUBLISHED, ALWAYS.\n=====================================================================\n(The body's open question: \"whether bill identity is index or a stable id —\nrwtest needs to name a bill across a save/load\". Cited from\n`BillVerbs.cs Configure` and `BillVerbs.cs SelectBills`.)\n\nNeither, alone. The verbs take `index | uid | recipe | all` — the same selector\n3.4's `surgery-remove` already takes, so the two bill surfaces speak one\nvocabulary — and every result row publishes BOTH.\n\n**`uid` is the durable one, and it is the game's own.**\n`Bill.GetUniqueLoadID()` is `\"Bill_\" + recipe.defName + \"_\" + loadID`, where\n`loadID` is `UniqueIDsManager.GetNextBillID()` assigned in the `Bill` ctor and\nscribed by `Bill.ExposeData` (`Scribe_Values.Look(ref loadID, \"loadID\")`). It\ntherefore survives save/load unchanged, which is precisely what the open\nquestion asked for. It is also what `Bill_Production.ExposeData`'s own\n`SaveSlotReferencable`/`LoadSlotReferencable` cross-references resolve against,\nso it is load-bearing inside the game and not a handle we invented.\n\n**`index` is NOT identity and the code says so out loud.** It is position in\n`BillStack.bills`, it is what `WorkGiver_DoBill` walks front-to-back\n(`BillStack.FirstShouldDoNow`), and it MOVES under `bill-reorder` — including\nunder someone else's `bill-reorder` between two of the agent's calls. Dropping\nit would have been wrong anyway: the whole POINT of `bill-reorder` is to address\na position, and \"move the bill at 3 to 0\" cannot be phrased in uids.\n\n**The corollary is the same one 1eb2262 reached for pawns, from the other\nside.** There, a stable EMIT ORDER was added so an index is reproducible, with\nthe stated limit that membership above the cap is not. Here the id is stable and\nthe ORDER is deliberately mutable, because reordering is a feature. The rule\nthat covers both: **an index is reproducible, never meaningful; hold the id when\nyou need the thing, use the index when you mean the place.** An acceptance\nscript naming a bill across an `advance` uses `uid` (3.6's suite does), and one\nproving a reorder uses `index` (it does that too).\n\n**Rejected alternative: `recipe` as the identity.** It is offered as a SELECTOR\nand it is genuinely useful (\"suspend every simple-meal bill\"), but a stack may\nhold fifteen bills of one recipe — that is what repeat modes are for — so it\nnames a SET, and `SelectBills` returns all matches for it. `bill-reorder`\nrefuses a selector matching anything but exactly one, by count, and says so.\n\n=====================================================================\nRESOLUTION 2 — `storage-set {copy_from}` BYPASSES `StorageSettingsClipboard`\nDELIBERATELY. THE CLIPBOARD IS A HUMAN'S UI STATE, NOT A TRANSPORT.\n=====================================================================\n(Cited from `StorageVerbs.cs`'s HAZARDS header. The body lists\n`StorageSettingsClipboard (:16,:23,:29)` as \"copy/paste for free\".)\n\nIt is not free; it costs the player's clipboard. `StorageSettingsClipboard.Copy`\nis `copiedSettings.CopyFrom(s)` plus a `Messages.Message` toast, and\n`PasteInto` is `s.CopyFrom(copiedSettings)` plus another toast, around one\nstatic `StorageSettings copiedSettings`. So routing an agent copy through it\nwould:\n\n- **CLOBBER a global the human owns.** `copiedSettings` is one static shared with\n  the actual ITab_Storage copy/paste buttons. An agent that copies a shelf's\n  filter silently destroys whatever the player had on their clipboard — a\n  side effect on UI state with no game-state justification, and invisible.\n- **cost two round trips** for one intention, when the agent is not holding a\n  clipboard between them and never wanted one.\n- **emit two toasts nothing reads.** Same reasoning already applied to\n  `storage-link`'s \"SettingsLinkedFor\" and `bill-add`'s two Dialog_MessageBoxes.\n\nWhat the clipboard pair actually DOES to game state is exactly one call —\n`StorageSettings.CopyFrom(other)`, which goes through the `Priority` PROPERTY\n(so haul invalidation fires) and `filter.CopyAllowancesFrom`, then\n`TryNotifyChanged`. `storage-set {copy_from:…}` makes that one call directly,\none round trip, and reports the source token in `changed`.\n\n**This is DESIGN's \"reproduce the helper's gate and its effect, and drop the\ntutorial line\" applied to a UI SCRATCHPAD rather than to a tutorial** — and the\ngeneralisation is worth having: *a vanilla helper whose only extra behaviour is\nwriting a static the PLAYER reads is not a helper for us; reproduce its effect\nand leave the human's state alone.* Same family as `storage-link`/`-unlink`\ntaking `targets` instead of reading `Find.Selector`, and for the same reason: a\nheadless player verb must not read or write the player's selection or clipboard.\n\n**Scope note, so nothing is silently missing:** there is no `storage-copy` /\n`storage-paste` verb pair and there should not be. `copy_from` is the whole\ncapability, it is plural over `targets` (paste to N storages in one call), and\na clipboard with nobody to look at it is a variable.\n\n=====================================================================\nRESOLUTION 3 — `bill-options` / `bill-add` REFUSE A NON-WORK-TABLE BILL GIVER,\nAND NAME THE ROUTE THAT OWNS IT.\n=====================================================================\n(Cited from `BillVerbs.cs`'s \"WHAT ABOUT OTHER IBILLGIVERS\" header. The body's\nscope line says \"add / remove / reorder / suspend on any `IBillGiver`\".)\n\nThe body asks for any `IBillGiver`; the ADD path cannot honour that without\nbecoming the god-hand this spec exists to prevent, so it is split by path\nrather than granted or refused wholesale.\n\n**Why the add path is work-table-only.** `RimWorld/ITab_Bills.cs SelTable` is a\nhard cast — `(Building_WorkTable)base.SelThing` — and every gate `bill-add`\nreproduces (`def.AllRecipes` as the universe, `AvailableNow`,\n`AvailableOnNow(SelTable)`, `DoListing`'s `Count \u003c 15`) is read off that tab.\nFor a bill giver that is NOT a `Building_WorkTable` there is no `ITab_Bills`,\ntherefore no widget, therefore **no gate to reproduce** — and DESIGN §Action\nmodel's rule is that reproducing a gate we have not read is exactly the failure.\n`BillStack.AddBill` would happily accept the bill and it would never be worked.\nSo `bill-options`/`bill-add` refuse with `gate:\"not-a-work-table\"` and name the\nowner:\n  * a Pawn's stack is its surgery queue (`Verse/Pawn.cs BillStack =\u003e\n    health.surgeryBills`) -\u003e 3.4's `surgery-options` / `surgery-add`, which\n    reproduce `HealthCardUtility.DrawMedOperationsTab`'s gate instead;\n  * a mech gestator / subcore scanner / modded giver has its OWN tab with its\n    own preconditions, unread -\u003e refused by name, and `bills` still READS it.\n`Building_WorkTableAutonomous` DERIVES from `Building_WorkTable`, so biofuel\nrefineries and the like are IN scope and take the same gate.\n\n**Why the ROW verbs are not restricted, which is the half the header got\nwrong until this round.** `bill-set` / `bill-reorder` / `bill-remove` gate on\n`IBillGiver`, not on `Building_WorkTable`, and that is correct and deliberate:\n`RimWorld/Bill.cs DoInterface` draws the suspend button, the reorder arrows and\nthe X in EVERY bill listing, the Health tab's included. A pawn IS reachable\n(`Verse/ThingListGroupHelper.cs` makes `ThingRequestGroup.PotentialBillGiver`\n`!def.AllRecipes.NullOrEmpty()`, and a humanlike race def has surgeries in\nAllRecipes — 3.4's own acceptance check 4.6a proves it live), so `BenchArg`\nresolves a pawn id and those three verbs work on a surgery queue. The\n`Dialog_BillConfig` levers are then refused BY NAME on a non-`Bill_Production`,\nbecause `Bill_Production.GetBillDialog()` is the only thing that opens that\nwindow. `BillVerbs.cs`'s class header asserted the opposite — \"medical bills on\na PAWN are deliberately NOT reachable from here\" — while `Configure`'s comment\ntwo hundred lines below said the true thing. The header is corrected; the\nbehaviour is unchanged and was right.","files":null}]}